jobs.description:
Are you experienced in a warehouse and ready to take the next step into a leadership role? Or do you already have some experience in supervising colleagues and want to further develop yourself as a team leader? Then this is your opportunity! Within a fast-growing and international logistics environment, you will have the opportunity to further develop your leadership skills and  take on more responsibility step by step.

As a (junior) Warehouse Team Leader, you will work alongside an experienced team and supervise a group of 10 to 12 employees. You will be visibly present on the work floor, supporting the daily coordination of operations. You work closely with the Supervisor and be given the space to grow in your role.

Your responsibilities include:

- Supporting the supervision and guidance of warehouse employees;
- Working on the floor to ensure smooth daily operations;
- Identifying operational bottlenecks and discussing them with your manager;
- Contributing to the improvement of work processes;
- Monitoring basic safety and quality regulations;
- Working with simple reports and developing basic Excel skills.

We are primarily looking for someone with the right motivation and ambition to grow into a leadership role within logistics. In addition, you have:

- Experience in a warehouse or logistics environment;
- Interest in supervising or guiding colleagues;
- Good command of the English language (required);
- Basic knowledge of Excel or willingness to learn;
- A proactive and eager-to-learn attitude;
- Availability to work full-time in a two-shift system.

Have you not yet held a full team leader position, but do you have ambition and some initial experience in leading others? We strongly encourage you to apply.

A leading Spanish organization in the comprehensive logistics sector with over 14,000 people in 21 countries is recruiting talent for their warehouse in Amsterdam.

What are you going to do?
•    Loading/unloading and build of air freight plates;
•    Sorting and scanning the freight;
•    Structure of shipments following the contours manuals and manifest;
•    Processing the air cargo;
•    Forklift activities
•    Keep the workplace nice and tidy;
•    Support the Team Leader in carrying out warehouse activities.

Who are we looking for?
•    Experience with air freight;
•    You are prepared to work in 3 shifts
•    VGB and Air Freight certificate;
•    You are able to speak English;
•    You are willing to work during the weekends.

What do we offer?
•    A competitive salary;
•    Possibility of a permanent contract in long-term;
•    Irregularity shift allowances of at least 35% up to 145% on top of your current hourly salary;
•    Overtime paid (30%) after 40 hours a week;
•    Pension premium free, (paid by employer);
•    8% holiday allowance;
•    Travel allowance of € 0.23 per kilometer;
•    26 paid vacation days per year;
•    An exciting, challenging, and independent job in a dynamic company with a direct and open communication culture and an informal atmosphere.

As a Production Employee, you will help ensure that food products are processed and packaged correctly. You will work together with colleagues to keep the production line running smoothly and check that products meet the required quality standards. Through your commitment, you contribute to an efficient production process and help maintain a safe and well-organized working environment.
What will you do?

• Package, label, and prepare food products for transport;
• Operate, monitor, and adjust machines when necessary during the production process;
• Inspect products for quality, packaging, and correct label information;
• Help maintain a clean and safe workplace in accordance with applicable guidelines;
• Work together with colleagues to successfully achieve production targets and planning requirements.

Functie-eisen:
- You can read and understand Dutch and/or English, enabling you to work safely and follow instructions correctly;
• You are willing to work at multiple production locations within the region and enjoy variety in your work;
• You are available for rotating shifts, including day, evening, and night shifts, for 16 to 32 hours per week;
• You quickly adapt to new tasks and enjoy learning how to work with different machines and production processes;
• You work accurately, pay attention to product quality, and contribute to maintaining a safe and clean working environment.
